 Retrieved November 25, 2021, pp. 192\\u2013194.\\nO.B. Akhmedova, Z.Z. Rakhimov. Technique for obtaining methyldiethanolamine, which is applied in the treatment of gases. Retrieved November 25, 2021, pp. 167\\u2013170.\\nSCIENTIFIC WORKS INCLUDED IN SCOPUS AND WEB OF SCIENCE\\nKayum Jumaev, Baxodir Tursunov. Technology for Obtaining Fuel Briquettes from Oil Waste. IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science, Krasnoyarsk, Russia, 16\\u201318 June 2022.\\nTEXTBOOKS AND MANUALS\\nM.Zh. Makhmudov and others. Modern methods of physicochemical analysis. 2024.\\nE.R. Panoyev and others. Catalytic processes and catalysts for petrochemical industry. 2025 year.\\nB.J Tursunov and others. Chemistry and physics of petroleum. 2025 year.\\nM.Q. Turakulova and others. Research Methodology. 2025 year.\\nS.F. Fozilov and others. Methods of physical and chemical analysis of oil and gas products. 2025 year.\\nMONOGRAPHS\\n\\u00abSmall biogas plants designed for the population and farms\\u00bb. Bukhara, 2021.\\n\\u00abActivated Charcoal for Organic Feedstock Gas Processing Plants\\u00bb. Bukhara, 2021.\\n\\\"Technology for Obtaining Polymethacrylate-Based Additives for Fuels and Oils\\\". Bukhara, 2020.\\n\\\"Obtaining effective solutions based on drilling muds\\\". Bukhara, 2020.\\n\\\"Motor Gasolines and Ways to Improve Their Sustainability.\\\" Tashkent, 2020.\",\"SCIENTIFIC AND METHODICAL WORK OF THE DEPARTMENT, SCIENTIFIC ARTICLES\\nIn cooperation with JSC \\\"Uzbekneftegaz\\\" and \\\"CISTU\\\" to provide laboratories with modern laboratory equipment and devices \\\"Scientific research\\\", \\\"Oil and gas business\\\" and \\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" with a total value of 3,5884 blrr. Soums. The total cost between BSTU and Bukhara Oil Refinery LLC amounted to 900 million sums. The contract was concluded until the end of 2024, and to date 900 mln. sum of funds has been paid by enterprise. The total value between BSTU and Bukhara Oil Refinery LLC amounted to 950 mln. The contract was concluded until the end of 2025. LLC \\\"Shurtan gas chemical complex\\\" presented 5 unused equipment.\\nIn order to purchase modern laboratory equipment and equipment for three laboratory rooms of the department, a list of laboratory equipment has been formed and the proposals of firms belonging to the Russian Federation, Germany-Uzbekistan C.K. \\\"Precision Technology\\\" LLC and Sharif University of Technology (Iran) have been studied. The total cost with Iran\'s Sharif Technological University is 186,000. Negotiations are underway to purchase 19 types of laboratory equipment worth US dollars.\\nA total amount of 5.4 billion rubles between the production enterprises of BSTU and JSC Uzbekneftegaz planned to be completed in 2024-2016. It is planned to draw up contracts for joint implementation of scientific projects - uzbeks. Mubaak Oil & Gas Production Authority (OPCW) received 1 2 billion rubles. soums, 3 2 billion rubles were donated to the Department of Gas Oil and Gas Production. 55 million. and \\\"Bukhara Oil Refinery\\\" LLC for 850 million sums. Drafts of contracts for Uzbek services are submitted.\\nDepartment of Oil and Gas Refining Technology Bukhara State Technical University Scientific council DSc.03\\/28.02.2022.T.101.01 for academic degrees in the following specialties: Chemistry and technology of oil and gas and technology and 02.00.11 - Chemistry of colloids and membranes. On April 26, 2025, Toshbaev Sardor Uktamovich, an independent researcher of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing, successfully completed the thesis recommended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in the specialty of Colloid and membrane chemistry on 02.00.11 \\u2013 Colloid and membrane chemistry on April 26, 2025. On June 13, 2025 she received her PhD diploma (Diploma number: 01No017877). On August 20, 2025, the senior lecturer of the department \\\"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" Hajiyeva Rukhsora Bakhtiyorovna successfully passed the thesis recommended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) on the topic \\\"Development of a scientific and technological basis for the process of removing fuel distillates from rubber and plastic waste\\\" 02.00.08 \\u2013 \\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\" (technical sciences), and on October 31, 2025 she received her PhD diploma (diploma number: 01No020097). On December 25, 2025, doctoral student of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology Akhmedova Shakhnoza UtkirovnaDevelopment of an effective absorbent composition for cleaning of products from sour components\\\" was defended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences on the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\". On December 25, 2025, Khamidov Dilshodjon Ganievich for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences in the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" on the topic \\\"Technology of obtaining base oil for plastic welding materials from local waste\\\" was held. On December 26, 2025, Hotamov Kabul Shirinboyich defended his thesis for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences on the specialty 02.00.08 \\u2013 \\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\" on the topic \\\"Development of technology for regeneration of used hydraulic oil using Navbahar bentonite\\\". On December 26, 2025, Tokhtayev Nazim Nazirovich defended his thesis for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences from the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" on the topic \\\"Development of technology for obtaining anti-detonation compositions based on broadcasts and their compounding with motor gasoline\\\".\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"Hamkorlik\",\"items\":[\"International relations and cooperation of the Department of Technology of Oil and Gas Processing Technology\\nIn order to ensure the execution of the Memorandum signed between Uzbekneftegaz JSC and the State Oil Company of the Republic of Azerbaijan (SOCAR) in the field of personnel training, a cooperation agreement was signed between Bukhara State Technical University and Baku Higher Oil School on the organization of a joint education program for master\'s degree. In the 2024\\/2025 academic year, as a result of entrance exams, 10 trainees were admitted, 7 continued their studies, 3 were dismissed due to family circumstances From April 7 to May 30, 2025, qualified faculty members of the University conducted classes in English. On June 12-14, 2018, responsible employees of Baku Higher Oil School visited the University and held master classes for masters studying under the joint educational program, giving instructions on preparing for the exam. On June 19-20, Aysel Rizaeva, head of the education quality department of Baku Higher Oil School, and Guldana Khidoyatli, vice-rector for strategic development, arrived at the University and took an exam in the subjects prescribed by the curriculum for 1 semester. According to the results of the examination, all seven masters were recommended to study in Baku Higher Oil School. Training processes will be organized in Azerbaijan on September 15, 2025, and the departure of masters to Baku is scheduled for September 8, 2025.\\nAccording to the project of the Erasmus + program \\\"101082221-UzMedEn - New Master\'s and Training Courses in the Field of Medical Engineering in Uzbekistan\\\", the lecturer of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology G. From September 27 to October 15, 2024, Zaripov successfully completed an internship at the prestigious Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VGTU), which is included in the TOP 1000 universities of Lithuania. Cooperation agreements were signed with the Atyrau Oil and Gas University named after S. Utebaev, Ufa State Oil Technical University and South Kazakhstan University named after M. Auezov for professional development, internships, postgraduate and doctoral studies for the teaching staff of the department in foreign educational institutions.\\nRepresentatives of Bukhara State Technical University Hayitov Ruslan Rustamjonovich and Bozorov Gairat Rashidovich also took part in the 33rd International Oil, Gas, Technology Exhibition and Forum of the Petrochemical Industry, which was held in Ufa, Russian Federation in May 2025.\\nFrom October 22 to November 4, 2024, senior researcher Ruslan Hayitov, Ph.D., associate degree in order to study teaching methods and acquire skills in Chinese higher education. Garyrat Bozorov, basic doctoral student Maxim Tsukanov took part in a refresher course for the program \\\"New Energy-Based Vehicles\\\" at the Hebei Professional University of Technology and Engineering (China). According to the memorandum of cooperation signed between our Institute and South Kazakhstan University named after M.Auezov (basis: letter of South Kazakhstan University named after M.Auezov No.1753\\/11 dated 28.11.2024) according to the memorandum of cooperation signed between our Institute and South Kazakhstan University named after M. AuezovTechnology of Inorganic and Petrochemical Production\\\" in accordance with the program of academic mobility gave lectures and practical lessons.\\nAccording to the project of the Erasmus + program \\\"101082221-UzMedEn - New Master\'s and Training Courses in the Field of Medical Engineering in Uzbekistan\\\", the lecturer of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology G. From September 27 to October 15, 2024, Zaripov successfully completed an internship at the prestigious Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VGTU), which is included in the TOP 1000 universities of Lithuania.\\nS.F.Fozilov, S.A.Gaibullayev, B.Z.Sharipov and M.Z.Komilov took an active part in an international foresight session on the topic \\\"Implementation of the concept of development of technical education: new trends in training modern engineers\\\" in order to increase the coverage of students in the field of oil and gas refining, increase their competitiveness and improve monitoring of their employment.\"]}]', 'Neft va gazni qayta ishlash texnologiyasi', 'Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified perso', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:46'),
(3, 1, 'ru', 'Технология переработки нефти и газа', 'Технология переработки нефти и газа', 'Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified personnel to the Bukhara oil refinery, the Mubarak gas refinery, the Gazlineftegaziburization department and other enterprises. Originally a PhD in Chemistry. M. Mardonov headed the department. From 2002 to 2009, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences Q.K.Jumaev. From 2009 to 2011, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences J.A.Qalandarov.\nOn April 15, 2013, in accordance with the decree PP-1954 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technical Institute\", the Department of \"Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing\" and \"Oil and Gas Business\" was formed from the merger of the departments \"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\" and \"Oil and Gas Business\". From that day until January 2, 2014, the department was headed by PhD in technical sciences B.Z.Adizov. From January 2, 2014 to July 20, 2014, Ph.D. Sharipov worked as acting head of the department. From July 20, 2014 to July 10, 2019, Professor G. R. Bozorov headed the department.\nOn July 10, 2019, three departments (\"Oil Refining Technology\", \"Gas Chemical Processing Technology\" and \"Oil and Gas Business\") were established on the basis of the Department of Petroleum and Gas Chemical Industry Technology, which was approved by the Ministry of Secondary Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan. From January 28, 2022, the department was headed by Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) A.A. Alimov, and from 2023 to 2025, associate professor Sh.N. Ataullayev.\nIn accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 No. PP-22 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara State Technical University\" from April 10, 2025, Ph.D. R.R. Hayitov worked as the head of the department. From September 13, 2025 to the present, the department has been headed by Ph.D., associate professor. A.A.Ochilov is in charge.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"\\u041e\\u0431\\u0437\\u043e\\u0440\",\"items\":[\"Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology       \\n\\nOchilov Abduraxim Abdurasulovich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 91 411 00 16\\n Email: ochilov82@gmail.ru\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"\\u0418\\u0441\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440\\u0438\\u044f \\u043a\\u0430\\u0444\\u0435\\u0434\\u0440\\u044b\",\"items\":[\"Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified personnel to the Bukhara oil refinery, the Mubarak gas refinery, the Gazlineftegaziburization department and other enterprises. Originally a PhD in Chemistry. M. Mardonov headed the department. From 2002 to 2009, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences Q.K.Jumaev. From 2009 to 2011, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences J.A.Qalandarov.\\nOn April 15, 2013, in accordance with the decree PP-1954 \\\"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technical Institute\\\", the Department of \\\"Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" and \\\"Oil and Gas Business\\\" was formed from the merger of the departments \\\"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" and \\\"Oil and Gas Business\\\". From that day until January 2, 2014, the department was headed by PhD in technical sciences B.Z.Adizov. From January 2, 2014 to July 20, 2014, Ph.D. Sharipov worked as acting head of the department. From July 20, 2014 to July 10, 2019, Professor G. R. Bozorov headed the department.\\nOn July 10, 2019, three departments (\\\"Oil Refining Technology\\\", \\\"Gas Chemical Processing Technology\\\" and \\\"Oil and Gas Business\\\") were established on the basis of the Department of Petroleum and Gas Chemical Industry Technology, which was approved by the Ministry of Secondary Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan. From January 28, 2022, the department was headed by Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) A.A. Alimov, and from 2023 to 2025, associate professor Sh.N. Ataullayev.\\nIn accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 No. PP-22 \\\"On the establishment of the Bukhara State Technical University\\\" from April 10, 2025, Ph.D. R.R. Hayitov worked as the head of the department. From September 13, 2025 to the present, the department has been headed by Ph.D., associate professor. A.A.Ochilov is in charge.\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"\\u041f\\u043e\\u0434\\u0433\\u043e\\u0442\\u0430\\u0432\\u043b\\u0438\\u0432\\u0430\\u0435\\u043c\\u044b\\u0435 \\u0441\\u043f\\u0435\\u0446\\u0438\\u0430\\u043b\\u0438\\u0441\\u0442\\u044b\",\"items\":[\"UNDERGRADUATE DEGREE\\n60721100 - Technology of oil and gas refining\\n60720500 \\u2013 Technology of Deep Gas Processing\\nJUDICIARY\\n70720600 - Technology of oil and gas processing\\nDOCTORAL DEGREE\\n02.00.08 - Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\"]},{\"key\":\"subjects\",\"title\":\"\\u041f\\u0440\\u0435\\u043f\\u043e\\u0434\\u0430\\u0432\\u0430\\u0435\\u043c\\u044b\\u0435 \\u0434\\u0438\\u0441\\u0446\\u0438\\u043f\\u043b\\u0438\\u043d\\u044b\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s Degree:\\n1. Introduction\\nto Specialization 2. Oil and Gas Processing Technology 1,2\\n3. Equipment and equipment for oil and gas processing 1,2\\n4. Design of enterprises of the oil and gas processing industry\\n5. General Chemical Technology\\n6. Synthesis and Technology of Monomers from Gas and Gas Condensate\\n7. Chemistry and Technology of Fuels and Oils\\n8. Disposal of oil and gas processing waste\\n9. Quality control of oil and gas\\nproducts 10. Modern methods of oil and gas product research\\n11. Physics and Chemistry of Natural Gas and Gas Condensates 1,2\\n12. Hydrocarbon Gas Processing Technology 1,2\\n13. Technology of\\nNatural Gas and Gas Condensate Processing 14. Chemistry and Technology of Polymer Processing\\n15. Synthesis and Technology of Monomers Based on Gases and Gas Condensate\\n16. Protection of metals from corrosion\\n17. Oil and Gas Refining\\nProcesses 18. Production of liquid hydrocarbons from gas using GTL technology in Uzbekistan 20. Petroleum-Gas Chemistry and Physics\\n19. Equipment and equipment of oil and gas refineries\\n20. Quality control of oil and gas\\nproducts 21. Chemistry and Technology of Synthetic and Biofuels\\nProduction 22. Equipment and equipment of oil and gas refineries\\n23. Deep Oil Refining Technology\\n24. Pyrolysis\\nof Hydrocarbon Feedstock 25. Physics and Chemistry of\\nHydrocarbon Gases 26. Operation of Oil Bases and Gas Stations\\n27. Energy Saving Technologies in Oil and Gas Refining\\nIndustry 28. Training on the processes of the oil and gas refining industry\\n29. Landings used in the petrochemical industry\\n30. Additional resources in the oil and gas chemical industry\\n31. Inorganic sorbents\\nof oil and gas refining 32. Catalyst in the Gas Chemical Industry 33. Technology of\\nSynthesis Gas Production 34. Gas Supply Systems 35. Use of gas distribution and disposal points 36. Process training of the gas chemical industry\\nJudiciary\\n1. Methodology of scientific research\\n2.Technology of deep processing of oil and gas 1,2\\n3.Corrosion protection\\nof oil and gas refining equipment 4.Improvement and design of oil and gas processing enterprises\\n5.Methods of teaching special disciplines\\n6.Research work and preparation of master\'s dissertation\\n7.Scientific and pedagogical work\\n8.Modern methods of physical and chemical analysis\\n9.Industrial technologies and innovations\\n10.Experimental planning\\n11.Chemistry of oil and gas refining products\\n12.Chemistry and technology of obtaining additives for fuels and oils\\n13.Chemistry of production of alternative and synthetic mature fuels\\n14.Chemistry and technology of natural gas-based syntheses\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"\\u041f\\u0440\\u043e\\u0444\\u0435\\u0441\\u0441\\u043e\\u0440\\u0441\\u043a\\u043e-\\u043f\\u0440\\u0435\\u043f\\u043e\\u0434\\u0430\\u0432\\u0430\\u0442\\u0435\\u043b\\u044c\\u0441\\u043a\\u0438\\u0439 \\u0441\\u043e\\u0441\\u0442\\u0430\\u0432 \\u043a\\u0430\\u0444\\u0435\\u0434\\u0440\\u044b\",\"items\":[\"Head of the department,\\nOchilov Abdurasulovich\",\"DSc,professor\\nMaxmudov Muxtor Jamolovich\",\"DSc, professor.\\nHayitov Ruslan Rustamjonovich\",\"DSc,professor\\nBozorov G\\u2018ayrat Rashidovich\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nXo\\u2018jaqulov Aziz Fayzullaevich\",\"t.f.n., dotsent\\nMurodov Malik Negmurodovich\",\"t.f.n., dotsent\\nSafarov Baxri Djumaevich\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nTsukanov Maksim Nikolayevich\"]},{\"key\":\"publications\",\"title\":\"\\u0423\\u0447\\u0435\\u0431\\u043d\\u0438\\u043a\\u0438 \\u0438 \\u0441\\u0442\\u0430\\u0442\\u044c\\u0438\",\"items\":[\"ABSTRACTS AND PAPERS FROM THE CONFERENCES (INTERNATIONAL AND REPUBLICAN)\\nJ.A. Safarov, R.R. Hayitov. The S&P 500 has been hit hard by the S&P 500 Index. \\\"The Politics and Politics of Nigeria...\\\" Proceedings of the National Conference-Symposium, November 25, 2021, pp. 165\\u2013167.\\n\\u0416.\\u0410. \\u0421\\u0430\\u0444\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0432, \\u0420.\\u0420. \\u04b2\\u0430\\u0439\\u0438\\u0442\\u043e\\u0432. \\u0418\\u0448\\u043b\\u0430\\u0442\\u0438\\u043b\\u0433\\u0430\\u043d \\u043c\\u043e\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440 \\u043c\\u043e\\u0439\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438\\u043d\\u0433 \\u0442\\u0430\\u0440\\u043a\\u0438\\u0431\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0430\\u043d\\u0438\\u049b\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448. \\u0412-\\u0425\\u0430\\u043b\\u049b\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e \\u043a\\u043e\\u043d\\u0444\\u0435\\u0440\\u0435\\u043d\\u0446\\u0438\\u044f-\\u0441\\u0438\\u043c\\u043f\\u043e\\u0437\\u0438\\u0443\\u043c, 25 \\u043d\\u043e\\u044f\\u0431\\u0440\\u044c 2021 \\u0439., 255\\u2013258 \\u0431.\\n\\u0416.\\u0410. \\u0421\\u0430\\u0444\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0432, \\u0420.\\u0420. \\u04b2\\u0430\\u0439\\u0438\\u0442\\u043e\\u0432. \\u0418\\u0448\\u043b\\u0430\\u0442\\u0438\\u043b\\u0433\\u0430\\u043d \\u043c\\u043e\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440 \\u043c\\u043e\\u0439\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u043e\\u0437\\u0430\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448 \\u0443\\u0441\\u0443\\u043b\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u0430\\u043d\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448. \\u0412-\\u0425\\u0430\\u043b\\u049b\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e \\u043a\\u043e\\u043d\\u0444\\u0435\\u0440\\u0435\\u043d\\u0446\\u0438\\u044f-\\u0441\\u0438\\u043c\\u043f\\u043e\\u0437\\u0438\\u0443\\u043c, 25 \\u043d\\u043e\\u044f\\u0431\\u0440\\u044c 2021 \\u0439., 258\\u2013261 \\u0431.\\n\\u0416.\\u0410. \\u0421\\u0430\\u0444\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0432, \\u041a.\\u0428. \\u04b2\\u043e\\u0442\\u0430\\u043c\\u043e\\u0432. \\u042e\\u049b\\u043e\\u0440\\u0438 \\u0441\\u0438\\u0444\\u0430\\u0442\\u043b\\u0438 \\u0434\\u0438\\u0437\\u0435\\u043b\\u044c \\u0451\\u049b\\u0438\\u043b\\u0493\\u0438\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0438\\u0448\\u043b\\u0430\\u0431 \\u0447\\u0438\\u049b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u0448 \\u0436\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u0451\\u043d\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438\\u043d\\u0433 \\u0437\\u0430\\u043c\\u043e\\u043d\\u0430\\u0432\\u0438\\u0439 \\u04b3\\u043e\\u043b\\u0430\\u0442\\u0438. \\u0422\\u043e\\u0448\\u043a\\u0435\\u043d\\u0442, 2021.\\n\\u041e.\\u0411. \\u0410\\u0445\\u043c\\u0435\\u0434\\u043e\\u0432\\u0430, \\u0417.\\u041d. \\u0410\\u043a\\u0440\\u0430\\u043c\\u043e\\u0432\\u0430. \\u0413\\u0430\\u0437\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u0430\\u0439\\u0451\\u0440\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448 \\u0436\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u0451\\u043d\\u0438\\u0434\\u0430 \\u043f\\u0430\\u0441\\u0442 \\u04b3\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0440\\u0430\\u0442\\u043b\\u0438 \\u0441\\u0435\\u043f\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u0430\\u0434\\u049b\\u0438\\u049b \\u049b\\u0438\\u043b\\u0438\\u0448. \\u0411\\u0443\\u0445\\u043e\\u0440\\u043e, 20\\u201322 \\u043e\\u043a\\u0442\\u044f\\u0431\\u0440\\u044c 2021 \\u0439., 326\\u2013327 \\u0431.\\nO.B. Akhmedova, Sh. Akhmedova. Gazlarni nordon komponentlardan tozalash uchun samarali absorbent compositionsini ishlab chikish. Bukhoro, October 20\\u201322, 2021, 328\\u2013329 p.\\nB.B. Toirov, A.A. Alimov. The relevance of production of synthetic petroleum feedstock from coal crude. Tashkent, 2022, pp. 135\\u2013137.\\nN.I. Bakhramov, O.B. Akhmedova, R.R. Hayitov. Investigation of the composition of granulated active charcoal for purification of alkanolamines. Retrieved November 25, 2021, pp. 192\\u2013194.\\nO.B. Akhmedova, Z.Z. Rakhimov. Technique for obtaining methyldiethanolamine, which is applied in the treatment of gases. Retrieved November 25, 2021, pp. 167\\u2013170.\\nSCIENTIFIC WORKS INCLUDED IN SCOPUS AND WEB OF SCIENCE\\nKayum Jumaev, Baxodir Tursunov. Technology for Obtaining Fuel Briquettes from Oil Waste. IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science, Krasnoyarsk, Russia, 16\\u201318 June 2022.\\nTEXTBOOKS AND MANUALS\\nM.Zh. Makhmudov and others. Modern methods of physicochemical analysis. 2024.\\nE.R. Panoyev and others. Catalytic processes and catalysts for petrochemical industry. 2025 year.\\nB.J Tursunov and others. Chemistry and physics of petroleum. 2025 year.\\nM.Q. Turakulova and others. Research Methodology. 2025 year.\\nS.F. Fozilov and others. Methods of physical and chemical analysis of oil and gas products. 2025 year.\\nMONOGRAPHS\\n\\u00abSmall biogas plants designed for the population and farms\\u00bb. Bukhara, 2021.\\n\\u00abActivated Charcoal for Organic Feedstock Gas Processing Plants\\u00bb. Bukhara, 2021.\\n\\\"Technology for Obtaining Polymethacrylate-Based Additives for Fuels and Oils\\\". Bukhara, 2020.\\n\\\"Obtaining effective solutions based on drilling muds\\\". Bukhara, 2020.\\n\\\"Motor Gasolines and Ways to Improve Their Sustainability.\\\" Tashkent, 2020.\",\"SCIENTIFIC AND METHODICAL WORK OF THE DEPARTMENT, SCIENTIFIC ARTICLES\\nIn cooperation with JSC \\\"Uzbekneftegaz\\\" and \\\"CISTU\\\" to provide laboratories with modern laboratory equipment and devices \\\"Scientific research\\\", \\\"Oil and gas business\\\" and \\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" with a total value of 3,5884 blrr. Soums. The total cost between BSTU and Bukhara Oil Refinery LLC amounted to 900 million sums. The contract was concluded until the end of 2024, and to date 900 mln. sum of funds has been paid by enterprise. The total value between BSTU and Bukhara Oil Refinery LLC amounted to 950 mln. The contract was concluded until the end of 2025. LLC \\\"Shurtan gas chemical complex\\\" presented 5 unused equipment.\\nIn order to purchase modern laboratory equipment and equipment for three laboratory rooms of the department, a list of laboratory equipment has been formed and the proposals of firms belonging to the Russian Federation, Germany-Uzbekistan C.K. \\\"Precision Technology\\\" LLC and Sharif University of Technology (Iran) have been studied. The total cost with Iran\'s Sharif Technological University is 186,000. Negotiations are underway to purchase 19 types of laboratory equipment worth US dollars.\\nA total amount of 5.4 billion rubles between the production enterprises of BSTU and JSC Uzbekneftegaz planned to be completed in 2024-2016. It is planned to draw up contracts for joint implementation of scientific projects - uzbeks. Mubaak Oil & Gas Production Authority (OPCW) received 1 2 billion rubles. soums, 3 2 billion rubles were donated to the Department of Gas Oil and Gas Production. 55 million. and \\\"Bukhara Oil Refinery\\\" LLC for 850 million sums. Drafts of contracts for Uzbek services are submitted.\\nDepartment of Oil and Gas Refining Technology Bukhara State Technical University Scientific council DSc.03\\/28.02.2022.T.101.01 for academic degrees in the following specialties: Chemistry and technology of oil and gas and technology and 02.00.11 - Chemistry of colloids and membranes. On April 26, 2025, Toshbaev Sardor Uktamovich, an independent researcher of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing, successfully completed the thesis recommended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in the specialty of Colloid and membrane chemistry on 02.00.11 \\u2013 Colloid and membrane chemistry on April 26, 2025. On June 13, 2025 she received her PhD diploma (Diploma number: 01No017877). On August 20, 2025, the senior lecturer of the department \\\"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" Hajiyeva Rukhsora Bakhtiyorovna successfully passed the thesis recommended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) on the topic \\\"Development of a scientific and technological basis for the process of removing fuel distillates from rubber and plastic waste\\\" 02.00.08 \\u2013 \\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\" (technical sciences), and on October 31, 2025 she received her PhD diploma (diploma number: 01No020097). On December 25, 2025, doctoral student of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology Akhmedova Shakhnoza UtkirovnaDevelopment of an effective absorbent composition for cleaning of products from sour components\\\" was defended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences on the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\". On December 25, 2025, Khamidov Dilshodjon Ganievich for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences in the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" on the topic \\\"Technology of obtaining base oil for plastic welding materials from local waste\\\" was held. On December 26, 2025, Hotamov Kabul Shirinboyich defended his thesis for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences on the specialty 02.00.08 \\u2013 \\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\" on the topic \\\"Development of technology for regeneration of used hydraulic oil using Navbahar bentonite\\\". On December 26, 2025, Tokhtayev Nazim Nazirovich defended his thesis for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences from the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" on the topic \\\"Development of technology for obtaining anti-detonation compositions based on broadcasts and their compounding with motor gasoline\\\".\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"\\u0421\\u043e\\u0442\\u0440\\u0443\\u0434\\u043d\\u0438\\u0447\\u0435\\u0441\\u0442\\u0432\\u043e\",\"items\":[\"International relations and cooperation of the Department of Technology of Oil and Gas Processing Technology\\nIn order to ensure the execution of the Memorandum signed between Uzbekneftegaz JSC and the State Oil Company of the Republic of Azerbaijan (SOCAR) in the field of personnel training, a cooperation agreement was signed between Bukhara State Technical University and Baku Higher Oil School on the organization of a joint education program for master\'s degree. In the 2024\\/2025 academic year, as a result of entrance exams, 10 trainees were admitted, 7 continued their studies, 3 were dismissed due to family circumstances From April 7 to May 30, 2025, qualified faculty members of the University conducted classes in English. On June 12-14, 2018, responsible employees of Baku Higher Oil School visited the University and held master classes for masters studying under the joint educational program, giving instructions on preparing for the exam. On June 19-20, Aysel Rizaeva, head of the education quality department of Baku Higher Oil School, and Guldana Khidoyatli, vice-rector for strategic development, arrived at the University and took an exam in the subjects prescribed by the curriculum for 1 semester. According to the results of the examination, all seven masters were recommended to study in Baku Higher Oil School. Training processes will be organized in Azerbaijan on September 15, 2025, and the departure of masters to Baku is scheduled for September 8, 2025.\\nAccording to the project of the Erasmus + program \\\"101082221-UzMedEn - New Master\'s and Training Courses in the Field of Medical Engineering in Uzbekistan\\\", the lecturer of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology G. From September 27 to October 15, 2024, Zaripov successfully completed an internship at the prestigious Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VGTU), which is included in the TOP 1000 universities of Lithuania. Cooperation agreements were signed with the Atyrau Oil and Gas University named after S. Utebaev, Ufa State Oil Technical University and South Kazakhstan University named after M. Auezov for professional development, internships, postgraduate and doctoral studies for the teaching staff of the department in foreign educational institutions.\\nRepresentatives of Bukhara State Technical University Hayitov Ruslan Rustamjonovich and Bozorov Gairat Rashidovich also took part in the 33rd International Oil, Gas, Technology Exhibition and Forum of the Petrochemical Industry, which was held in Ufa, Russian Federation in May 2025.\\nFrom October 22 to November 4, 2024, senior researcher Ruslan Hayitov, Ph.D., associate degree in order to study teaching methods and acquire skills in Chinese higher education. Garyrat Bozorov, basic doctoral student Maxim Tsukanov took part in a refresher course for the program \\\"New Energy-Based Vehicles\\\" at the Hebei Professional University of Technology and Engineering (China). According to the memorandum of cooperation signed between our Institute and South Kazakhstan University named after M.Auezov (basis: letter of South Kazakhstan University named after M.Auezov No.1753\\/11 dated 28.11.2024) according to the memorandum of cooperation signed between our Institute and South Kazakhstan University named after M. AuezovTechnology of Inorganic and Petrochemical Production\\\" in accordance with the program of academic mobility gave lectures and practical lessons.\\nAccording to the project of the Erasmus + program \\\"101082221-UzMedEn - New Master\'s and Training Courses in the Field of Medical Engineering in Uzbekistan\\\", the lecturer of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology G. From September 27 to October 15, 2024, Zaripov successfully completed an internship at the prestigious Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VGTU), which is included in the TOP 1000 universities of Lithuania.\\nS.F.Fozilov, S.A.Gaibullayev, B.Z.Sharipov and M.Z.Komilov took an active part in an international foresight session on the topic \\\"Implementation of the concept of development of technical education: new trends in training modern engineers\\\" in order to increase the coverage of students in the field of oil and gas refining, increase their competitiveness and improve monitoring of their employment.\"]}]', 'Технология переработки нефти и газа', 'Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified perso', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:46'),
(4, 1, 'ar', 'تكنولوجيا تكرير النفط والغاز', 'تكنولوجيا تكرير النفط والغاز', 'Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified personnel to the Bukhara oil refinery, the Mubarak gas refinery, the Gazlineftegaziburization department and other enterprises. Originally a PhD in Chemistry. M. Mardonov headed the department. From 2002 to 2009, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences Q.K.Jumaev. From 2009 to 2011, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences J.A.Qalandarov.\nOn April 15, 2013, in accordance with the decree PP-1954 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technical Institute\", the Department of \"Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing\" and \"Oil and Gas Business\" was formed from the merger of the departments \"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\" and \"Oil and Gas Business\". From that day until January 2, 2014, the department was headed by PhD in technical sciences B.Z.Adizov. From January 2, 2014 to July 20, 2014, Ph.D. Sharipov worked as acting head of the department. From July 20, 2014 to July 10, 2019, Professor G. R. Bozorov headed the department.\nOn July 10, 2019, three departments (\"Oil Refining Technology\", \"Gas Chemical Processing Technology\" and \"Oil and Gas Business\") were established on the basis of the Department of Petroleum and Gas Chemical Industry Technology, which was approved by the Ministry of Secondary Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan. From January 28, 2022, the department was headed by Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) A.A. Alimov, and from 2023 to 2025, associate professor Sh.N. Ataullayev.\nIn accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 No. PP-22 \"On the establishment of the Bukhara State Technical University\" from April 10, 2025, Ph.D. R.R. Hayitov worked as the head of the department. From September 13, 2025 to the present, the department has been headed by Ph.D., associate professor. A.A.Ochilov is in charge.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"\\u0646\\u0638\\u0631\\u0629 \\u0639\\u0627\\u0645\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology       \\n\\nOchilov Abduraxim Abdurasulovich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 91 411 00 16\\n Email: ochilov82@gmail.ru\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"\\u062a\\u0627\\u0631\\u064a\\u062e \\u0627\\u0644\\u0642\\u0633\\u0645\",\"items\":[\"Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified personnel to the Bukhara oil refinery, the Mubarak gas refinery, the Gazlineftegaziburization department and other enterprises. Originally a PhD in Chemistry. M. Mardonov headed the department. From 2002 to 2009, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences Q.K.Jumaev. From 2009 to 2011, the department was headed by PhD of Technical Sciences J.A.Qalandarov.\\nOn April 15, 2013, in accordance with the decree PP-1954 \\\"On the establishment of the Bukhara Engineering and Technical Institute\\\", the Department of \\\"Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" and \\\"Oil and Gas Business\\\" was formed from the merger of the departments \\\"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" and \\\"Oil and Gas Business\\\". From that day until January 2, 2014, the department was headed by PhD in technical sciences B.Z.Adizov. From January 2, 2014 to July 20, 2014, Ph.D. Sharipov worked as acting head of the department. From July 20, 2014 to July 10, 2019, Professor G. R. Bozorov headed the department.\\nOn July 10, 2019, three departments (\\\"Oil Refining Technology\\\", \\\"Gas Chemical Processing Technology\\\" and \\\"Oil and Gas Business\\\") were established on the basis of the Department of Petroleum and Gas Chemical Industry Technology, which was approved by the Ministry of Secondary Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan. From January 28, 2022, the department was headed by Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) A.A. Alimov, and from 2023 to 2025, associate professor Sh.N. Ataullayev.\\nIn accordance with the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated January 24, 2025 No. PP-22 \\\"On the establishment of the Bukhara State Technical University\\\" from April 10, 2025, Ph.D. R.R. Hayitov worked as the head of the department. From September 13, 2025 to the present, the department has been headed by Ph.D., associate professor. A.A.Ochilov is in charge.\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u062e\\u0635\\u0635\\u0627\\u062a \\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u064a \\u064a\\u062a\\u0645 \\u0625\\u0639\\u062f\\u0627\\u062f\\u0647\\u0627\",\"items\":[\"UNDERGRADUATE DEGREE\\n60721100 - Technology of oil and gas refining\\n60720500 \\u2013 Technology of Deep Gas Processing\\nJUDICIARY\\n70720600 - Technology of oil and gas processing\\nDOCTORAL DEGREE\\n02.00.08 - Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\"]},{\"key\":\"subjects\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u0645\\u0642\\u0631\\u0631\\u0627\\u062a \\u0627\\u0644\\u062f\\u0631\\u0627\\u0633\\u064a\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s Degree:\\n1. Introduction\\nto Specialization 2. Oil and Gas Processing Technology 1,2\\n3. Equipment and equipment for oil and gas processing 1,2\\n4. Design of enterprises of the oil and gas processing industry\\n5. General Chemical Technology\\n6. Synthesis and Technology of Monomers from Gas and Gas Condensate\\n7. Chemistry and Technology of Fuels and Oils\\n8. Disposal of oil and gas processing waste\\n9. Quality control of oil and gas\\nproducts 10. Modern methods of oil and gas product research\\n11. Physics and Chemistry of Natural Gas and Gas Condensates 1,2\\n12. Hydrocarbon Gas Processing Technology 1,2\\n13. Technology of\\nNatural Gas and Gas Condensate Processing 14. Chemistry and Technology of Polymer Processing\\n15. Synthesis and Technology of Monomers Based on Gases and Gas Condensate\\n16. Protection of metals from corrosion\\n17. Oil and Gas Refining\\nProcesses 18. Production of liquid hydrocarbons from gas using GTL technology in Uzbekistan 20. Petroleum-Gas Chemistry and Physics\\n19. Equipment and equipment of oil and gas refineries\\n20. Quality control of oil and gas\\nproducts 21. Chemistry and Technology of Synthetic and Biofuels\\nProduction 22. Equipment and equipment of oil and gas refineries\\n23. Deep Oil Refining Technology\\n24. Pyrolysis\\nof Hydrocarbon Feedstock 25. Physics and Chemistry of\\nHydrocarbon Gases 26. Operation of Oil Bases and Gas Stations\\n27. Energy Saving Technologies in Oil and Gas Refining\\nIndustry 28. Training on the processes of the oil and gas refining industry\\n29. Landings used in the petrochemical industry\\n30. Additional resources in the oil and gas chemical industry\\n31. Inorganic sorbents\\nof oil and gas refining 32. Catalyst in the Gas Chemical Industry 33. Technology of\\nSynthesis Gas Production 34. Gas Supply Systems 35. Use of gas distribution and disposal points 36. Process training of the gas chemical industry\\nJudiciary\\n1. Methodology of scientific research\\n2.Technology of deep processing of oil and gas 1,2\\n3.Corrosion protection\\nof oil and gas refining equipment 4.Improvement and design of oil and gas processing enterprises\\n5.Methods of teaching special disciplines\\n6.Research work and preparation of master\'s dissertation\\n7.Scientific and pedagogical work\\n8.Modern methods of physical and chemical analysis\\n9.Industrial technologies and innovations\\n10.Experimental planning\\n11.Chemistry of oil and gas refining products\\n12.Chemistry and technology of obtaining additives for fuels and oils\\n13.Chemistry of production of alternative and synthetic mature fuels\\n14.Chemistry and technology of natural gas-based syntheses\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"\\u0623\\u0639\\u0636\\u0627\\u0621 \\u0647\\u064a\\u0626\\u0629 \\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u062f\\u0631\\u064a\\u0633 \\u0641\\u064a \\u0627\\u0644\\u0642\\u0633\\u0645\",\"items\":[\"Head of the department,\\nOchilov Abdurasulovich\",\"DSc,professor\\nMaxmudov Muxtor Jamolovich\",\"DSc, professor.\\nHayitov Ruslan Rustamjonovich\",\"DSc,professor\\nBozorov G\\u2018ayrat Rashidovich\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nXo\\u2018jaqulov Aziz Fayzullaevich\",\"t.f.n., dotsent\\nMurodov Malik Negmurodovich\",\"t.f.n., dotsent\\nSafarov Baxri Djumaevich\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nTsukanov Maksim Nikolayevich\"]},{\"key\":\"publications\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u0643\\u062a\\u0628 \\u0648\\u0627\\u0644\\u0645\\u0642\\u0627\\u0644\\u0627\\u062a\",\"items\":[\"ABSTRACTS AND PAPERS FROM THE CONFERENCES (INTERNATIONAL AND REPUBLICAN)\\nJ.A. Safarov, R.R. Hayitov. The S&P 500 has been hit hard by the S&P 500 Index. \\\"The Politics and Politics of Nigeria...\\\" Proceedings of the National Conference-Symposium, November 25, 2021, pp. 165\\u2013167.\\n\\u0416.\\u0410. \\u0421\\u0430\\u0444\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0432, \\u0420.\\u0420. \\u04b2\\u0430\\u0439\\u0438\\u0442\\u043e\\u0432. \\u0418\\u0448\\u043b\\u0430\\u0442\\u0438\\u043b\\u0433\\u0430\\u043d \\u043c\\u043e\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440 \\u043c\\u043e\\u0439\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438\\u043d\\u0433 \\u0442\\u0430\\u0440\\u043a\\u0438\\u0431\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0430\\u043d\\u0438\\u049b\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448. \\u0412-\\u0425\\u0430\\u043b\\u049b\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e \\u043a\\u043e\\u043d\\u0444\\u0435\\u0440\\u0435\\u043d\\u0446\\u0438\\u044f-\\u0441\\u0438\\u043c\\u043f\\u043e\\u0437\\u0438\\u0443\\u043c, 25 \\u043d\\u043e\\u044f\\u0431\\u0440\\u044c 2021 \\u0439., 255\\u2013258 \\u0431.\\n\\u0416.\\u0410. \\u0421\\u0430\\u0444\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0432, \\u0420.\\u0420. \\u04b2\\u0430\\u0439\\u0438\\u0442\\u043e\\u0432. \\u0418\\u0448\\u043b\\u0430\\u0442\\u0438\\u043b\\u0433\\u0430\\u043d \\u043c\\u043e\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440 \\u043c\\u043e\\u0439\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u043e\\u0437\\u0430\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448 \\u0443\\u0441\\u0443\\u043b\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u0430\\u043d\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448. \\u0412-\\u0425\\u0430\\u043b\\u049b\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e \\u043a\\u043e\\u043d\\u0444\\u0435\\u0440\\u0435\\u043d\\u0446\\u0438\\u044f-\\u0441\\u0438\\u043c\\u043f\\u043e\\u0437\\u0438\\u0443\\u043c, 25 \\u043d\\u043e\\u044f\\u0431\\u0440\\u044c 2021 \\u0439., 258\\u2013261 \\u0431.\\n\\u0416.\\u0410. \\u0421\\u0430\\u0444\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0432, \\u041a.\\u0428. \\u04b2\\u043e\\u0442\\u0430\\u043c\\u043e\\u0432. \\u042e\\u049b\\u043e\\u0440\\u0438 \\u0441\\u0438\\u0444\\u0430\\u0442\\u043b\\u0438 \\u0434\\u0438\\u0437\\u0435\\u043b\\u044c \\u0451\\u049b\\u0438\\u043b\\u0493\\u0438\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0438\\u0448\\u043b\\u0430\\u0431 \\u0447\\u0438\\u049b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u0448 \\u0436\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u0451\\u043d\\u043b\\u0430\\u0440\\u0438\\u043d\\u0438\\u043d\\u0433 \\u0437\\u0430\\u043c\\u043e\\u043d\\u0430\\u0432\\u0438\\u0439 \\u04b3\\u043e\\u043b\\u0430\\u0442\\u0438. \\u0422\\u043e\\u0448\\u043a\\u0435\\u043d\\u0442, 2021.\\n\\u041e.\\u0411. \\u0410\\u0445\\u043c\\u0435\\u0434\\u043e\\u0432\\u0430, \\u0417.\\u041d. \\u0410\\u043a\\u0440\\u0430\\u043c\\u043e\\u0432\\u0430. \\u0413\\u0430\\u0437\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u0430\\u0439\\u0451\\u0440\\u043b\\u0430\\u0448 \\u0436\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u0451\\u043d\\u0438\\u0434\\u0430 \\u043f\\u0430\\u0441\\u0442 \\u04b3\\u0430\\u0440\\u043e\\u0440\\u0430\\u0442\\u043b\\u0438 \\u0441\\u0435\\u043f\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u0442\\u043e\\u0440\\u043d\\u0438 \\u0442\\u0430\\u0434\\u049b\\u0438\\u049b \\u049b\\u0438\\u043b\\u0438\\u0448. \\u0411\\u0443\\u0445\\u043e\\u0440\\u043e, 20\\u201322 \\u043e\\u043a\\u0442\\u044f\\u0431\\u0440\\u044c 2021 \\u0439., 326\\u2013327 \\u0431.\\nO.B. Akhmedova, Sh. Akhmedova. Gazlarni nordon komponentlardan tozalash uchun samarali absorbent compositionsini ishlab chikish. Bukhoro, October 20\\u201322, 2021, 328\\u2013329 p.\\nB.B. Toirov, A.A. Alimov. The relevance of production of synthetic petroleum feedstock from coal crude. Tashkent, 2022, pp. 135\\u2013137.\\nN.I. Bakhramov, O.B. Akhmedova, R.R. Hayitov. Investigation of the composition of granulated active charcoal for purification of alkanolamines. Retrieved November 25, 2021, pp. 192\\u2013194.\\nO.B. Akhmedova, Z.Z. Rakhimov. Technique for obtaining methyldiethanolamine, which is applied in the treatment of gases. Retrieved November 25, 2021, pp. 167\\u2013170.\\nSCIENTIFIC WORKS INCLUDED IN SCOPUS AND WEB OF SCIENCE\\nKayum Jumaev, Baxodir Tursunov. Technology for Obtaining Fuel Briquettes from Oil Waste. IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science, Krasnoyarsk, Russia, 16\\u201318 June 2022.\\nTEXTBOOKS AND MANUALS\\nM.Zh. Makhmudov and others. Modern methods of physicochemical analysis. 2024.\\nE.R. Panoyev and others. Catalytic processes and catalysts for petrochemical industry. 2025 year.\\nB.J Tursunov and others. Chemistry and physics of petroleum. 2025 year.\\nM.Q. Turakulova and others. Research Methodology. 2025 year.\\nS.F. Fozilov and others. Methods of physical and chemical analysis of oil and gas products. 2025 year.\\nMONOGRAPHS\\n\\u00abSmall biogas plants designed for the population and farms\\u00bb. Bukhara, 2021.\\n\\u00abActivated Charcoal for Organic Feedstock Gas Processing Plants\\u00bb. Bukhara, 2021.\\n\\\"Technology for Obtaining Polymethacrylate-Based Additives for Fuels and Oils\\\". Bukhara, 2020.\\n\\\"Obtaining effective solutions based on drilling muds\\\". Bukhara, 2020.\\n\\\"Motor Gasolines and Ways to Improve Their Sustainability.\\\" Tashkent, 2020.\",\"SCIENTIFIC AND METHODICAL WORK OF THE DEPARTMENT, SCIENTIFIC ARTICLES\\nIn cooperation with JSC \\\"Uzbekneftegaz\\\" and \\\"CISTU\\\" to provide laboratories with modern laboratory equipment and devices \\\"Scientific research\\\", \\\"Oil and gas business\\\" and \\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" with a total value of 3,5884 blrr. Soums. The total cost between BSTU and Bukhara Oil Refinery LLC amounted to 900 million sums. The contract was concluded until the end of 2024, and to date 900 mln. sum of funds has been paid by enterprise. The total value between BSTU and Bukhara Oil Refinery LLC amounted to 950 mln. The contract was concluded until the end of 2025. LLC \\\"Shurtan gas chemical complex\\\" presented 5 unused equipment.\\nIn order to purchase modern laboratory equipment and equipment for three laboratory rooms of the department, a list of laboratory equipment has been formed and the proposals of firms belonging to the Russian Federation, Germany-Uzbekistan C.K. \\\"Precision Technology\\\" LLC and Sharif University of Technology (Iran) have been studied. The total cost with Iran\'s Sharif Technological University is 186,000. Negotiations are underway to purchase 19 types of laboratory equipment worth US dollars.\\nA total amount of 5.4 billion rubles between the production enterprises of BSTU and JSC Uzbekneftegaz planned to be completed in 2024-2016. It is planned to draw up contracts for joint implementation of scientific projects - uzbeks. Mubaak Oil & Gas Production Authority (OPCW) received 1 2 billion rubles. soums, 3 2 billion rubles were donated to the Department of Gas Oil and Gas Production. 55 million. and \\\"Bukhara Oil Refinery\\\" LLC for 850 million sums. Drafts of contracts for Uzbek services are submitted.\\nDepartment of Oil and Gas Refining Technology Bukhara State Technical University Scientific council DSc.03\\/28.02.2022.T.101.01 for academic degrees in the following specialties: Chemistry and technology of oil and gas and technology and 02.00.11 - Chemistry of colloids and membranes. On April 26, 2025, Toshbaev Sardor Uktamovich, an independent researcher of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing, successfully completed the thesis recommended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in the specialty of Colloid and membrane chemistry on 02.00.11 \\u2013 Colloid and membrane chemistry on April 26, 2025. On June 13, 2025 she received her PhD diploma (Diploma number: 01No017877). On August 20, 2025, the senior lecturer of the department \\\"Technology of Oil and Gas Processing\\\" Hajiyeva Rukhsora Bakhtiyorovna successfully passed the thesis recommended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) on the topic \\\"Development of a scientific and technological basis for the process of removing fuel distillates from rubber and plastic waste\\\" 02.00.08 \\u2013 \\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\" (technical sciences), and on October 31, 2025 she received her PhD diploma (diploma number: 01No020097). On December 25, 2025, doctoral student of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology Akhmedova Shakhnoza UtkirovnaDevelopment of an effective absorbent composition for cleaning of products from sour components\\\" was defended for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences on the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\". On December 25, 2025, Khamidov Dilshodjon Ganievich for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences in the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" on the topic \\\"Technology of obtaining base oil for plastic welding materials from local waste\\\" was held. On December 26, 2025, Hotamov Kabul Shirinboyich defended his thesis for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences on the specialty 02.00.08 \\u2013 \\\"Chemistry and technology of oil and gas\\\" on the topic \\\"Development of technology for regeneration of used hydraulic oil using Navbahar bentonite\\\". On December 26, 2025, Tokhtayev Nazim Nazirovich defended his thesis for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in technical sciences from the specialty 02.00.08-\\\"Oil and gas chemistry and technology\\\" on the topic \\\"Development of technology for obtaining anti-detonation compositions based on broadcasts and their compounding with motor gasoline\\\".\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u0639\\u0627\\u0648\\u0646\",\"items\":[\"International relations and cooperation of the Department of Technology of Oil and Gas Processing Technology\\nIn order to ensure the execution of the Memorandum signed between Uzbekneftegaz JSC and the State Oil Company of the Republic of Azerbaijan (SOCAR) in the field of personnel training, a cooperation agreement was signed between Bukhara State Technical University and Baku Higher Oil School on the organization of a joint education program for master\'s degree. In the 2024\\/2025 academic year, as a result of entrance exams, 10 trainees were admitted, 7 continued their studies, 3 were dismissed due to family circumstances From April 7 to May 30, 2025, qualified faculty members of the University conducted classes in English. On June 12-14, 2018, responsible employees of Baku Higher Oil School visited the University and held master classes for masters studying under the joint educational program, giving instructions on preparing for the exam. On June 19-20, Aysel Rizaeva, head of the education quality department of Baku Higher Oil School, and Guldana Khidoyatli, vice-rector for strategic development, arrived at the University and took an exam in the subjects prescribed by the curriculum for 1 semester. According to the results of the examination, all seven masters were recommended to study in Baku Higher Oil School. Training processes will be organized in Azerbaijan on September 15, 2025, and the departure of masters to Baku is scheduled for September 8, 2025.\\nAccording to the project of the Erasmus + program \\\"101082221-UzMedEn - New Master\'s and Training Courses in the Field of Medical Engineering in Uzbekistan\\\", the lecturer of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology G. From September 27 to October 15, 2024, Zaripov successfully completed an internship at the prestigious Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VGTU), which is included in the TOP 1000 universities of Lithuania. Cooperation agreements were signed with the Atyrau Oil and Gas University named after S. Utebaev, Ufa State Oil Technical University and South Kazakhstan University named after M. Auezov for professional development, internships, postgraduate and doctoral studies for the teaching staff of the department in foreign educational institutions.\\nRepresentatives of Bukhara State Technical University Hayitov Ruslan Rustamjonovich and Bozorov Gairat Rashidovich also took part in the 33rd International Oil, Gas, Technology Exhibition and Forum of the Petrochemical Industry, which was held in Ufa, Russian Federation in May 2025.\\nFrom October 22 to November 4, 2024, senior researcher Ruslan Hayitov, Ph.D., associate degree in order to study teaching methods and acquire skills in Chinese higher education. Garyrat Bozorov, basic doctoral student Maxim Tsukanov took part in a refresher course for the program \\\"New Energy-Based Vehicles\\\" at the Hebei Professional University of Technology and Engineering (China). According to the memorandum of cooperation signed between our Institute and South Kazakhstan University named after M.Auezov (basis: letter of South Kazakhstan University named after M.Auezov No.1753\\/11 dated 28.11.2024) according to the memorandum of cooperation signed between our Institute and South Kazakhstan University named after M. AuezovTechnology of Inorganic and Petrochemical Production\\\" in accordance with the program of academic mobility gave lectures and practical lessons.\\nAccording to the project of the Erasmus + program \\\"101082221-UzMedEn - New Master\'s and Training Courses in the Field of Medical Engineering in Uzbekistan\\\", the lecturer of the Department of Oil and Gas Processing Technology G. From September 27 to October 15, 2024, Zaripov successfully completed an internship at the prestigious Vilnius Gediminas Technical University (VGTU), which is included in the TOP 1000 universities of Lithuania.\\nS.F.Fozilov, S.A.Gaibullayev, B.Z.Sharipov and M.Z.Komilov took an active part in an international foresight session on the topic \\\"Implementation of the concept of development of technical education: new trends in training modern engineers\\\" in order to increase the coverage of students in the field of oil and gas refining, increase their competitiveness and improve monitoring of their employment.\"]}]', 'تكنولوجيا تكرير النفط والغاز', 'Since 2001-2002 academic year on the basis of Bukhara Autonomous Okrug and Yesti, the Department of Technologies of Oil and Gas Processing has been organized. The purpose of the creation of the department in this region was to provide qualified perso', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:46'),
(5, 2, 'en', 'Food Technology and Service', 'Food Technology and Service', 'In accordance with the decree of the Ministry of Higher and Secondary Special Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. 6 of 1980, the department \"Technology of bread, pasta and confectionery products\" was organized. Since August 28, 2017, according to the new structure of the institute, the name of \"Food Technology\" was renamed into the Department of 5321000-Food Technology (by branches) of the uniting specialty in the areas of undergraduate education.', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"Overview\",\"items\":[\"Department of Food Technology and Service     \\n\\nFood processing technology and service\\n\\nQurbonov Murod Tashpulatovich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Shanba (15:00-17:00)\\n Phone: +998 90 299 85 48\\n Email: kurbanov.m@rambler.ru\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"Department History\",\"items\":[\"In accordance with the decree of the Ministry of Higher and Secondary Special Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. 6 of 1980, the department \\\"Technology of bread, pasta and confectionery products\\\" was organized. Since August 28, 2017, according to the new structure of the institute, the name of \\\"Food Technology\\\" was renamed into the Department of 5321000-Food Technology (by branches) of the uniting specialty in the areas of undergraduate education.\",\"He has held the following positions in the areas of food technology education: Dos at the Department of \\\"Technology of Bread, Pasta and Confectionery Products\\\". Vosiev M.G., dos. Mokhnacheva A.I., I.B. Isabaev (1980-2011). Department of \\\"Technology of grain storage and processing\\\" dos. T\\u0131ndybekov O. T., dos. Lavrinovich. Yu.I., dos. Ismatov N.A., dos. Boboev S.D. et al. Khaitov R.A., Adizov R.T. (1981-2013)\",\"Head of the department \\\"Technology of oil and oil products\\\" prof. Majidov.Q.X. (1990-2010). \\\"Technology of common catering and its organization\\\", then the heads of the department \\\"Food Safety\\\" prof. Egamberdiev N.B., prof. Makhmadaliev B.D., prof. Sharifulina T.A., prof. Salomov H.T., dos. Salomov B.H. and dos. Quliev N.Sh. (1981-2013)\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"Professor-Teachers of the Department\",\"items\":[\"Candidate of the Technical Science Associate Professor\\nAtamuradova Tamara Ivanovna\",\"Candidate of Technical Sciences, Associate Professor\\nErgasheva Khusrabo Bobonazarovna\",\"Candidate of the technical sciences:\\nassociate professor Khaydarzoda Lolitta Negmatovna\",\"Candidate of the technical sciences, associate professor (PhD)\\nKhuzhakulova Nilufar Fayzullayevna\",\"kata teacher\\nYuldasheva Shabon Jumaevna\",\"Candidate of technical sciences, associate professor (PhD)\\nIsmatova Shakhnoza Nusratillonovna\",\"assistent\\/strong>\\nAmonov Bobur Nematovich\",\"Assistant\\nMuzafarova Hall Mukhinovna\",\"Head of the Cabinet Khamroyev\\nJonibek Sadilloyevich\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"Prepared Specialists\",\"items\":[\"UNDERGRADUATE DEGREE\\n60720100 \\u2013 Food technology. 1st Course\\n1. Fundamentals of modern professional technology\\n2. The composition and properties of plant raw materials\\n60720300 \\u2013 Technology of wine growing, whisking products and soft drinks\\n1. Fundamentals of modern professional technology\\n2. The composition and properties of plant raw materials\\n60720400 \\u2013 Conservation Technology\\n1. Fundamentals of modern professional technology\\n2. The composition and properties of plant raw materials\\n60720100 \\u2013 Food technology. 2nd course\\n1.Food biochemistry\\n2.Food commodity science 3.Food\\nexamination\\n4.Food raw materials and materials\\ncommodity science 5.Food microbiology\\n6.Physicochemical methods of determining the quality of food products\\n60720300 \\u2013 Technology of wine growing, whisking products and soft drinks\\n1.Food commodity science\\n2.Food microbiology\\n60720400 \\u2013 Conservation Technology\\n1.Food biochemistry\\n2.Food commodity science\\n3.Food microbiology and biotechnology\\n4.Physicochemical methods of determining the quality of food products\\n5321000-Food technology(by types of products). Course 3\\n1. Food Research\\nMethods 2. Raw materials and nutritional additives in the production of bread, pasta and confectionery\\nproducts 3. Wisdom\\n4. Food Quality\\nAssessment 5. Bakery, pasta and confectionery equipment\\n6. Technology of\\nPasta Products 7. Technology of production of confectionery\\nproducts 8. Flour and Technologies of Production\\n9. Equipment of\\ngrain processing enterprises 10. Technology of storage of grain and grain products\\n5321000-Food technology (by type of products). Course 4\\n1. Examination of bread, pasta and confectionery\\nproducts 2. Confectionery Products Technology\\n3. Bread Biochemistry\\n4. Technical and chemical control of bread, pasta and confectionery products\\n5. Feed production technology in Omixta\\n6. Examination of Grain and Grain Products\\n7. Technology of\\nstorage of grain and grain products 8. Elevator and Warehouse\\n9. Basics of financing industrial enterprises\\n70720101-Technology of production and processing of food products (types of products)\\n1. Grain Biochemistry\\n2. Innovations in the technology of production of confectionery, bread and pasta\\nproducts 3. Scientific basis for improving the efficiency and competitiveness of food production from vegetable raw\\nmaterials 4. Ventilation and pneumatic transport\\ndevices 5. Scientific and pedagogical work\\n6. Research work and preparation of a master\'s thesis\\n7. Current trends in technology development in the food industry\\n8. Use of biotechnology advances in agricultural processing\\n9. Scientific Foundations of Un-Baking Technology\\n10. Seed processing\\n11. The Elevator-Warehouse Industry and Grain Drying\\n12. Scientific practice (gaining experience)\\nJUDICIARY\\n70720101 \\u2013 Technology of processing and processing of food products (bakery products)\\n70720101 \\u2013 Technology of processing and processing of food products (grain products)\"]},{\"key\":\"activities\",\"title\":\"Activities of the Department\",\"items\":[\"The faculty of the Department of Food Technology use innovative techniques and technologies available in our laboratory rooms, deeply teaching students their knowledge and qualifications, contributing to their future becoming a mature specialist. In addition, a number of research works are conducted by the department\'s researchers. Much progress has been made in this regard.\",\"Photos from the training on the HACCP system, organized by the Association of Food Industry of Uzbekistan, the Bukhara Engineering and Technological Institute and the German organization GIZ\",\"Photos from the cultural and educational event on the occasion of the 580th anniversary of Alisher Navoi, which was held together with the senior teacher of the department \\\"Food and Food Technology\\\" Sh.J. Yuldasheva and 1st year students and magists.\",\"A photo from the process of gaining experience at JSC \\\"Kogondon Products\\\" with graduate students of the department Associate Professor Ergasheva Kh.B. and senior teacher Yuldasheva Sh.J. with graduate students of the department.\",\"Associate Professor of the Department of Food Technology N.R.Djuraeva took part in the contest \\\"Inventive Woman-2022\\\" and became the winner in the nomination \\\"The Best Invention and Useful Model\\\".\",\"On the initiative of the Department of Food Technology, the children of the House of Muruvvat were informed about the festive mood and dresses made of national adras fabric and a holiday was organized.\"]},{\"key\":\"publications\",\"title\":\"Textbooks and Articles\",\"items\":[\"MONOGRAPHS\\n1. The monograph \\\"Technological properties of the wheat of Uzbekistan\\\" was published by Kh.B.Ergasheva, Sh.J.Yuldasheva.\\n2. Kh.B.Ergasheva, Sh.J.Yuldasheva published a monograph \\\"Rations of feeding agricultural animals\\\".\\n3. Kh.B.Ergasheva, Sh.J.Yuldasheva, Sh.N.Ismatova published a monograph entitled \\\"Research of the process of storing kombikorov in the conditions of Uzbekistan\\\".\\nTEXTBOOKS:\\n1. S.Ravshanov, N.A.Ismatov, Sh.J.Yuldasheva prepared a textbook on the topic \\\"Modern technologies of flour and oat production\\\" and on the basis of the order of the Ministry of Higher and Secondary Special Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. 1000 dated December 7, 2018, the grade 100-117 was taken.\\n2. Kh.B.Ergasheva, Sh.J.Yuldasheva, G.Z.Djakhangirova, M.T.Kurbanov prepared a textbook on the topic \\\"Biochemistry of the Grain\\\" which was obtained in accordance with the order of the Ministry of Higher and Secondary Special Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. 237 dated May 31, 2021.\\n3. H.B.Ergasheva, M.B. Kamolova \\\"Professional ethics and etiquette\\\". Textbook. Bukhara regional printing house Bukhara, 2020. 260 b.\\n\\u018flaq\\u0259\\n1. Kh.B.Ergasheva Technology of feed production in Omix (textbook) Bukhara: \\\"Bukhara edition\\\" Publishing House, 2019. 230b.\\n2. N.A.Ismatov, S.D.Boboev, Sh.Zh.Yuldasheva \\\"Aspiration and ventilation devices\\\" textbooks. Tashkent, \\\"Interpretation\\\" publishing house\",\"Articles\\n1.Ergasheva H.B. Research of Change in Humidity of Local and Other Varieties of Soya Seeds at Various Storage Modes. Annals of R.S.C.B., ISSN:1583-6258, Vol. 25, Issue 3, 2021, Pages. 7039 - 7047 Received 16 February 2021; Accepted 08 March 2021. http:\\/\\/annalsofrscb.\\n2. Ergasheva H.B. The Effect Of Drinking And Activated Water On Field Scales Of Wheat Grains Grown In Arid Climatic Conditions. European Journal of Molecular & Clinical Medicine ISSN 2515-8260 Volume 07, Issue 03, 2020. \\u0420.3065-3068.\\n3. Amanov B.N. Influence of Products from Tomato Press on The Efficiency of The Technological Process and The Quality of Rye Bread \\/ B.N. Amanov, I.B.Isabaev, T.I. Atamuratova, I.Sh. Sadykov \\/\\/European Journal 