ic journal-Austria,Vienna. 2019. P. 28-31.\\n19. S.K.Jabborova Analysis of food value of non-traditional sugar substitutes for flour confectionery goods \\/ S.K.Jabborova, I.B.Isabaev, T.I.Atamuratova, L.N.Khaidar-Zadeh,U.M.Ibrahimov\\/\\/ Asian Journal of Multidimensional Research. (AJMR)http:tarj.in , aprel 2020.P. 162-171.\\n20. S.K.Jabborova Application of products of processing mulberries and roots of sugar beet in the production of cupcakes \\/ S.K.Jabborova, I.B.Isabaev, N.R.Djuraeva, M.T.Kurbanov, L.N.Khaidar-Zadeh, K.S.Rakhmonov \\/\\/ Journal of Critical Reviews ,ISSN-2394-5125 , Vol 7, Issue 9, 2020. P.277-286.\\n21. S.K.Jabborova, I.B.Isabaev, I.Sh. Sadikov Methods to prevent silken powder collapsing and clushing during storage \\/ S.K.Jabborova, I.B.Isabaev, , I.Sh. Sadikov \\/\\/ Middle European scientific bulletin Volume 5. October 2020.P.166-170.\\n22. S.K.Jabborova Use of Silk Berries and Sugar Beet Roots in the Production of Muffins\\/ S.K.Jabborova \\/\\/ International Journal of Innovative Research in Science, Engineering and Technology (IJIRSET) Volume 10, Issue 12, December 2021.P.15102-15112.\\n23. S.K.Jabborova Silk Berries Beet Roots in The Production of Muffins \\/ S.K.Jabborova \\/\\/ Texas Journal of Multidisciplinary Studies, In Volume 3, 14-12-2021. P.139-140\\n24. \\u041a\\u0443\\u0440\\u0431\\u043e\\u043d\\u043e\\u0432 \\u041c.\\u0422. Improvement of the design of mobile equipment for post-harvest processing of agricultural crops.\\/ \\u041a\\u0443\\u0440\\u0431\\u043e\\u043d\\u043e\\u0432 \\u041c.\\u0422.,\\u0411\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u043a\\u0430\\u0435\\u0432 \\u041d.\\u0420., \\u0411\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430\\u043a\\u0430\\u0435\\u0432 \\u0410.\\u041d.,\\n25.Djuraeva N.R. Method for rational use of botanical oil content in wheat germ product\\/ Djuraeva N.R., Tursunova U.O\\/\\/ Asian Journal of Multidimensional Research (AJMR) https:\\/\\/www.tarj.in ISSN: 2278-4853 Vol 10, Issue 9, September, 2021 Impact Factor: SJIF 2021 = 7.699.\"]},{\"key\":\"research\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u0623\\u0639\\u0645\\u0627\\u0644 \\u0627\\u0644\\u0628\\u062d\\u062b\\u064a\\u0629\",\"items\":[\"International grants and projects\\nRegional program \\\"Vocational education in Central Asia \\u2013 I\\\" in 2010-2021 organized by the German Society for International Cooperation (Deutsche Gesellschaft f\\u00fcr Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) GmbH on behalf of the Federal Ministry of Economic Cooperation and Development of the Federal Republic of Germany, since 2018 the head of the Institute Kurbanov M.T. and members of the department Prof. Isabaev I.B., dos. Kuliyev N.Sh., dos. Atamuratova T.I., Ph.D. Azimov O\'N., PhD. Djuraeva N.R., Jabborova S.K. have passed international internship (advanced training) in the disciplines of \\\"Food Technology\\\" in the leading universities of Central Asia. According to this project 5 modern laboratory units are fully equipped.\\nDuring the period of project activity the following investments were made to the department:\\n1. A modern production laboratory \\\"Food technology \\\" is established and training is being conducted External investment was made for educational laboratory furniture (Microbiology, Sensor and Analytical analysis rooms) for 2.148 000 000 UZS Laboratory equipment was provided in the amount of 3.37 000 Euro. Equipped with household appliances and computer equipment for 4.50 000 000 UZS.\\nFor 2022-2023, within the framework of the GIZ-German International Cooperation Organization project \\\"Opening Uzbekistan to the world of wine (OUWOW)\\\", in cooperation with the University of Coimbra, Portugal, in the amount of 200,000 euros, was funded for new teaching materials and advanced training for the field of education \\\"Wine technology\\\".\\nThe department has relations with Dresden State Technical University (Germany), Moscow State University of Food Production (Russia), Tajikistan State Technical University, Osh State Technical University (Kyrgyzstan) and has concluded friendship agreements and is carrying out scientific and practical work.\\nOn the basis of a joint program with Mogilyaov State Food University of the Republic of Belarus, a memorandum was signed on the organization of advanced training and internships for professors and teachers on the basis of a bilateral diploma \\\"Bachelor\'s degree in food production\\\".\\nTeaching staff of the department working within the framework of the practical project PZ-2019062124 \\\"Creating technology for the production of mass food products using natural decontaminations\\\" (2022-2023). Funding -400 mln. UZS.\\nFood consumption is of very important importance in human life. However, the widespread use of modern intensive technologies, the use of chemicals and other non-food additives can be one of the main causes of food spoilage, including their biochemical changes and microbial damage and poisoning.\\nThe development of unprofitable microflora leads to spoilage of finished products, causing significant economic losses for both producers and consumers.\\nCertain biotechnologically and chemical methods of decontamination have microbostatic characteristics which sometimes fail to ensure the required quality of the product. Research on technological and cost-effective methods of decontamination of products in hot climates is an actual issue, has scientific and practical value.\\nThe practical project \\\"Development of technology for the production of functionally oriented flour, oats and bakery products\\\" is planned for 2023-2024. The amount of funding is 1,740 billion soums. The\\nproject is aimed at studying the current importance of functional food products, their role and comparative analysis in developed countries, the development of a technology for the production of functionally oriented flour, oatmeal and bread products based on local raw materials, the differences between the developed products and rational food products and the prophylactic and therapeutic properties.\\nCooperative Enterprise \\\"Oltin Ear \\u2013 Hot Bread\\\" LLC is undertaking an award of 50 mln sum on the theme \\\"Development of new types of rye bread recipes and technologies\\\". Commercial contract No. 44-22 was concluded.\\nThe members of the department in cooperation with Tanxo Shirin Servis LLC are working on the topic \\\"Development of Technologies of Flour Products Functional Purpose\\\". Irreplaceable substance increases micronutrients in raw materials, improves the quality of extracted products, improves their nutritional value. Work is underway to improve the composition of cake and biscuit products by adding natural fruits, produce a vitamin-rich product with reduced calorie content, and develop a product recipe. Test batches of the product are being produced.\\nDoctoral student of our department Djuraeva N.R. conducts scientific work on the theme: \\\"Scientific and practical aspects of targeted combination of raw materials in the production of vegetable and oil mixtures\\\". The thesis work is the development of scientifically based recipes and resource-saving technologies of vegetable-oil composition mixtures, the biopotential of which is predicted in advance, while the rational use of natural additives with natural stabilizers that increase the physiological value of bread and bakery products, quality indicators, shelf life, save the basic raw materials. The subject of the research was the development of innovative resource-intensive technology for the production of functional plant-fat compositions using environmentally friendly plant raw materials, while the object of the research was oils and vegetable oils, flax, soybean products, emulsion and anhydrous oil-and-paste mixtures, bread and flour products.\\nThe department conducts scientific work by the basic doctoral student Muzafarova H.M. on the theme: \\\"The use of unconventional raw materials in the development of new recipes for flour confectionery products for heroditic nutrition.\\\" In the development and creation of functional foods for herodietary purposes, one should know the chemical composition, nutritional value and special processing techniques of raw materials. In this context, the urgent task facing all branches of the food industry is to expand the range of products of food for herodietic purpose and improve technology through the use of natural, affordable raw materials and materials that meet the requirements of nutrition. The thesis proposes an approach to solutions, consisting of practical recommendations for the use of unconventional raw materials in the development of new recipes for bakery products for herodietic nutrition, which provides an increase in biotechnological potential, sets scientific tasks and substantiates it.\\nAssistant of the department Ismatova Sh.N. conducts scientific work on the theme: \\\"Rational use of non-traditional means in feed feed\\\". The purpose of the study is to improve the technology of production of feed with high nutritional value using unconventional feed means. The objectives of the research are to analyze and systematize modern data on improving productivity and reproductive qualities of poultry when using unconventional feed and feed additives, to select and substantiate raw material components for feed in the feed, to study their chemical composition, functional and technological properties and nutritional safety, to study the dried quinoa and amaranth grains (seeds) It consists of the development of technological parameters for unconventional methods of preparation and determination of the optimal dosage for their inclusion in the diet of chickens, as well as the study of the growth and development of poultry, meatiness, egg productivity and reproductive properties when using feed with added unconventional additives.\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u0639\\u0627\\u0648\\u0646\",\"items\":[\"For the renovation of the scientific laboratory of the department in 2019-2020 with the help of the program \\\"Vocational education in Central Asia-I\\\", 3 new laboratories worth 36 thousand euros were equipped, 150 million soums worth furniture and 60 million soums new equipment.\",\"Within the framework of the project \\\"Opening Uzbekistan to the World of Wine (OUWOW)\\\" in cooperation with the University of Coimbra, Portugal, 2022-2023 Educational direction \\\"Wine technology\\\" for 200 000 euros Funded for new teaching materials and professional development.\",\"JOINT PROGRAMS\\nMoscow State University of Food Production (MGUPP), Russian Federation\",\"Republic of Belarus, Mogilyov State University of Food and Chemical Technologies\",\"Latvian University of Natural Sciences and Technology, The Republic of Latvia\"]}]', 'تكنولوجيا الأغذية والخدمات', 'In accordance with the decree of the Ministry of Higher and Secondary Special Education of the Republic of Uzbekistan No. 6 of 1980, the department \"Technology of bread, pasta and confectionery products\" was organized. Since August 28, 2017, accordin', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:46'),
(9, 3, 'en', 'Chemical Technology', 'Chemical Technology', 'The department trains personnel in 2 areas of undergraduate education: 60710100 - Chemical technology (organic substances, inorganic substances, silicate materials, high molecular compounds), 60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes and 70710100 - Chemical technology of high-molecular compounds (by type of production) and 70710101 - Chemical technology (production of organic compounds).', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"Overview\",\"items\":[\"Department of Chemical Engineering      \\n\\nDepartment of Chemical Technology\\n\\nAxmedov Voxid Nizomovich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 90 511 59 58\\n Email: vohid7@mail.ru\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"Department History\",\"items\":[\"The department trains personnel in 2 areas of undergraduate education: 60710100 - Chemical technology (organic substances, inorganic substances, silicate materials, high molecular compounds), 60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes and 70710100 - Chemical technology of high-molecular compounds (by type of production) and 70710101 - Chemical technology (production of organic compounds).\",\"In these areas work 45 professors and teaching staff, including 4 professors, 24 PhD, associate professors, whose scientific potential is 60%. The department has 2 foreign language languages and 47 taught subjects. At present, the department trains 2 doctoral students, 28 basic doctoral students and 4 masters.\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"Professor-Teachers of the Department\",\"items\":[\"Head of the department:\\nAkhmedov Voksi Nizomovich\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nMakhmudov Rafiq Amonovich\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nTemirova Matlab Ibodovna\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nHaydarov Akhtam Amonovich\",\"PhD, associate professor\\nOlimov Babir Bahodir ugly\",\"PhD,associate professor\\nPanoyev Nadir Shavkatovich\",\"PhD, associate professor\\nSadikova Muxayyo Murodovna\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nSharipov Begmurod Sharopovich\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nUmarov Bobur Nosir o\'gli\",\"PhD, associate professor\\nKhuzhakulova Dilbar Jorakulovna\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nNarzullaeva Aziza Murodillayevna\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nVoxidov Erkin Aliyevich\",\"Assistent\\nJo\\u2018raeva Laylo Raxmatillaevna\",\"Assistent\\nSharipova Nasiba O\\u2018ktamovna\",\"Assistent\\nRaxmatov Marat Salimovich\",\"Assistent\\nSadikova Mashhura Idilloevna\",\"Assistent\\nG\\u2018afurova Gulnoz Alixonovna\",\"Assistent\\nJumaev Jabbor Hamroqulovich\",\"Teacher, trainee\\nIkromov Ulugbek Gafur oglu\",\"Teacher trainee\\nKurbonova Salima Shukhratovna\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"Prepared Specialists\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s degree\\n60710100 \\u2013 Chemical technology (chemical technology of inorganic substances)\\n60710100 \\u2013 Chemical technology (Silicate and Hard-to-Melt Nonmetallic Materials)\\n60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes;\\n60710100 - Chemical Technology (Organic Substances)\\n60710100 \\u2013 Chemical Technology (High Molecular Compounds)\\nJudiciary\\n70710101- Chemical technology of inorganic substances\\n70710101- Technology of silicate and hardly soluble nonmetallic materials;\\n70710101- Technology of mineral fertilizers\\n70710103 \\u2013 \\\"Chemical technology of high molecular weight compounds (technology of polymer production)\\n70710101 - Chemical technology (production of organic compounds)\\nPhD\\n02.00.11-\\\"Chemistry of colloids and membranes\\\"\\n02.00.13-\\\"Technology of inorganic substances and materials based on them\\\"\\n02.00.14-\\\"Technology of organic substances and materials based on them\\\"\\n02.00.16 \\u2013 Chemical technology, processes and devices of food industry\\n02.00.17 \\u2013 Technologies and biotechnologies for processing, storage and processing of agricultural and food products\"]},{\"key\":\"subjects\",\"title\":\"Taught Subjects\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s Degree:\\n1. Fundamentals of Construction of Manufacturing Enterprises\\n2. Bonded nitrogen production technology\\n3. Ammonium nitrate production technology\\n4. Modern methods of physicochemical analysis\\n5. Chemical technology of inorganic substances\\n6. Enterprise equipment\\n7. Thermal Processes and Devices in the Production of Silicate Materials\\n8. Fast Click Methods Technology\\n9. General Technology of Silicates\\n10. Prepress Technologies and Equipment\\n11. Pulp and papermaking technology\\n12. Technology of printing materials\\n13. Packaging Process Technologies and Equipment\\n14. Technology of silicate materials\\n15. Fundamentals of organic synthesis\\n16. Material hunos candy\\n17. Synthesis of organic matter\\n18. Organic Synthesis Equipment\\n19. Waste-free technologies in organic synthesis\\n20. Chemistry and technology of organic substances\\n21. Basics of Financing Organic Synthesis Enterprises\\n22. Synthetic Detergent Production Technology\\n23. Equipment for the production of synthetic detergents\\n24. Methods for the synthesis of monomers\\n25. Chemistry and Physics of High Molecular Compounds\\n26.Technology of coating-forming polymers\\n27.Classification of polymer materials and their fields of application\\n28.Technology of production of high molecular weight compounds\\n29.Chemistry\\n30.Chemistry (general and inorganic chemistry, analytical chemistry, physical-colloid chemistry)\\n31.Analytical and physical-colloid chemistry\\n32.Organic cumin\\n33.Construction chemistry\\n34.Organic and physical chemistry in construction\\n35Physico-colloid chemistry\\n36.Physical chemistry\\nJudiciary\\n1. Technological processes in the production of silicate materials\\n2. Theory and technological calculations of the production of mineral fertilizers\\n3. Theory and Technological Accounts of the Production of Inorganic Substances\\n4. Theory and technological calculations of the production of synthesized gases\\n5. Theory and technological calculations of bonded nitrogen production\\n6. Chemical technology of mineral fertilizers\\/ Chemical technology of potash salts\\n7. Chemistry and Technology of Element Organic Compounds\\n8. Adjustment of structure and properties in the manufacturing process of high-molecular compounds\\n9. Theoretical foundations of chemistry of high molecular weight compounds\\n10. Chemistry and technology of methane-based syntheses\\n11. Chemical theoretical foundations of coating-forming polymers\\n12. Technology of organic substances and materials based on them\\n13. Catalytic processes in the technology of obtaining organic products\\n14. Fundamentals of Physics and Mechanics of High Molecular Compounds\",\"Textbooks\\nTEXTBOOKS AND MANUALS\\n1. V.N.Akhmedov, Z.Kh.Rayimov, G.A.Gafurova.\\\" Terephthalic acid derivatives\\\". Monograph, Eastern-Bukhara Publishing House, Bukhara-2022.\\n2. Nurilloyev Zafar Ismatilloyevich, Asrayev Zafar Rizakulovich, Khojiyev Azizjon Kholmurodovich. \\\"Problems of general and inorganic chemistry and methods of their solution\\\" electronic textbook. DGU No. 40483.\\n3. Makhmudov Rafiq Amonovich, Shukrullaev Javohir Aibek ugli. \\\"Modern methods of physical and chemical analysis\\\". DGU No. 23886.\\n4. R.A.MAkhmudov, Ch.K.Khayrullayev, S.A.Niyozov, M.F.Haydarova, Z.M. Kamolova. \\\"Theory and Technological Accounts of Bonded Nitrogen Production.\\\" Textbook, ISBN 978-9943-9338-9-7. HOPE Publishing, 2023.\\n5. R.A.MAkhmudov, Z.M. Kamolova, S.A.Niyozov.\\\" Technology of Bonded Nitrogen and Nitrogen Fertilizers\\\". Monograph, UDK.667.664.3. 2024 6\\n. Niyozova N.R., Khuzhakulov K.R. \\\"Modification and application of synthetic oils in leather industry\\\". Monograph. ISBN 978-9943-8785-1-8. HOPE Publishing, 2023 7\\n. Sadirova S.N., Temirova M.I. Monograph, \\\"Effective technological approach in processing Karakul skins\\\". HOPE Publishing 2023.\\n8. Khaidarov A.A.\\\" \\u041f\\u043e\\u043b\\u0438\\u043c\\u0435\\u0440\\u044b \\u043d\\u0430 \\u043e\\u0441\\u043d\\u043e\\u0432\\u0435 \\u0445\\u0438\\u0442\\u0438\\u043d\\u0430 \\u0438 \\u0445\\u0438\\u0442\\u043e\\u0437\\u0430\\u043d\\u0430\\u201d. \\u041c\\u043e\\u043d\\u043e\\u0433\\u0440\\u0430\\u0444\\u0438\\u044f. \\u0418\\u0437\\u0434\\u0430\\u0442\\u0435\\u043b\\u044c\\u0441\\u0442\\u0432\\u043e \\u201c\\u0414\\u0443\\u0440\\u0434\\u043e\\u043d\\u0430\\u201d \\u0411\\u0443\\u0445\\u0430\\u0440\\u0430-2023\\u0433\\n9. Ostonov F.I,. Akhmedov V.N., Fayzullaev N.I., Dzhuraeva L.R., Olimov B.B. \\\"Chemistry and technology of polymers\\\". Textbook, No132760, 14.04.2025y\\n10. E.Kh.Atoev 60710100 - Direction of education: Chemical technology (by type of production) Chemistry of elements textbook. Order No. 55 of 04 March 2024\"]},{\"key\":\"research\",\"title\":\"Research Work\",\"items\":[\"02.00.11 - Specialty \\\"Chemistry of colloids and membranes\\\":\\n1. Teshayeva Marjona Samurodovna - Development of a scientific technological bases for obtaining activated coal from domestic raw materials for purification of kerosene fraction;\\n2.Tursunova Feruza Jamshidovna - Development of a process of sorption purification of water from fulvic acids using synthetic anionites;\\n3.Ikromov Ulug\'bek Gafur oglu - Synthesis of organic metals of established properties and study of colloidal chemical properties.\\n02.00.13 - Specialty of \\\"Technology of inorganic substances and materials based on them\\\":\\n1. Shodiyev Sobir Vahobjonovich - Properties and technology of obtaining hybrid compounds forming an inorganic-organic coating.\\n2. Fatilloyev Shamshod Fayzullo oglu - Development of technology for obtaining low-release nitrogen fertilizers based on\\nurea 3. Bakhshilloyev Nazim Komilovich-\\\"Effective use\\nof waste from mineral salts in the production of agricultural products 02.00.14 - \\\"Technology of organic substances and materials based on them\\\":\\n1. Sadullaeva Gulmira Gaibulloevna - \\\"Synthesis and properties of compounds based on hydroxybenzoic acids, fragments of amino acids and imidazole\\\"\\n2. Murodov Javlonbek Zafar oglu - Development of technology for obtaining bitumen emulsions on the basis of synthesis and modification of surfactants\\n02.00.16 - \\\"Technology of chemistry and processes and devices of food production\\\"\\n1.Shukrullaev Javohir Aibek ogli - Acceleration\\nof drying process by improving the flow structure of dispersible products 2.Dehkanova Nargiza Abduganievna - Improvement of alkaline neutralization equipment of vegetable oils by improving hydrodynamics of liquid phases.\\n02.00.17 - \\\"Technologies and biotechnologies of processing, storage and processing of agricultural and food products\\\"\\n1. Majidova Shakhnoza Bakhtiyorovna - \\\"The use of high-performance adsorbents in the technology of bleaching vegetable oils\\\"\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"Cooperation\",\"items\":[\"The department cooperates with South Kazakhstan State University, Volgograd Medical University, Saratov State University.\",\"Assoc. Prof. K.E.Rozieva in the library of South Kazakhstan State University.\",\"In the 2019-2021 academic year, on the basis of a joint program with the University of South Kazakhstan named after M. Auezova, service educational areas were opened and lessons are conducted by the department\'s teachers.\",\"NEWS IN THE DEPARTMENT\"]}]', 'Chemical Technology', 'The department trains personnel in 2 areas of undergraduate education: 60710100 - Chemical technology (organic substances, inorganic substances, silicate materials, high molecular compounds), 60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:46'),
(10, 3, 'uz', 'Kimyoviy texnologiya', 'Kimyoviy texnologiya', 'The department trains personnel in 2 areas of undergraduate education: 60710100 - Chemical technology (organic substances, inorganic substances, silicate materials, high molecular compounds), 60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes and 70710100 - Chemical technology of high-molecular compounds (by type of production) and 70710101 - Chemical technology (production of organic compounds).', '[{\"key\":\"overview\",\"title\":\"Umumiy ma\\u02bclumot\",\"items\":[\"Department of Chemical Engineering      \\n\\nDepartment of Chemical Technology\\n\\nAxmedov Voxid Nizomovich\\n Reception time: Dushanba-Juma (14:00-16:00 gacha)\\n Phone: +998 90 511 59 58\\n Email: vohid7@mail.ru\"]},{\"key\":\"history\",\"title\":\"Kafedra tarixi\",\"items\":[\"The department trains personnel in 2 areas of undergraduate education: 60710100 - Chemical technology (organic substances, inorganic substances, silicate materials, high molecular compounds), 60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes and 70710100 - Chemical technology of high-molecular compounds (by type of production) and 70710101 - Chemical technology (production of organic compounds).\",\"In these areas work 45 professors and teaching staff, including 4 professors, 24 PhD, associate professors, whose scientific potential is 60%. The department has 2 foreign language languages and 47 taught subjects. At present, the department trains 2 doctoral students, 28 basic doctoral students and 4 masters.\"]},{\"key\":\"staff\",\"title\":\"Kafedra professor-o\\u2018qituvchilari\",\"items\":[\"Head of the department:\\nAkhmedov Voksi Nizomovich\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nMakhmudov Rafiq Amonovich\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nTemirova Matlab Ibodovna\",\"Doctor of Technical Sciences, Professor\\nHaydarov Akhtam Amonovich\",\"PhD, associate professor\\nOlimov Babir Bahodir ugly\",\"PhD,associate professor\\nPanoyev Nadir Shavkatovich\",\"PhD, associate professor\\nSadikova Muxayyo Murodovna\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nSharipov Begmurod Sharopovich\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nUmarov Bobur Nosir o\'gli\",\"PhD, associate professor\\nKhuzhakulova Dilbar Jorakulovna\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nNarzullaeva Aziza Murodillayevna\",\"PhD, dotsent\\nVoxidov Erkin Aliyevich\",\"Assistent\\nJo\\u2018raeva Laylo Raxmatillaevna\",\"Assistent\\nSharipova Nasiba O\\u2018ktamovna\",\"Assistent\\nRaxmatov Marat Salimovich\",\"Assistent\\nSadikova Mashhura Idilloevna\",\"Assistent\\nG\\u2018afurova Gulnoz Alixonovna\",\"Assistent\\nJumaev Jabbor Hamroqulovich\",\"Teacher, trainee\\nIkromov Ulugbek Gafur oglu\",\"Teacher trainee\\nKurbonova Salima Shukhratovna\"]},{\"key\":\"prepared_specialists\",\"title\":\"Tayyorlanadigan mutaxassislar\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s degree\\n60710100 \\u2013 Chemical technology (chemical technology of inorganic substances)\\n60710100 \\u2013 Chemical technology (Silicate and Hard-to-Melt Nonmetallic Materials)\\n60710300 - Technology of printing and packaging processes;\\n60710100 - Chemical Technology (Organic Substances)\\n60710100 \\u2013 Chemical Technology (High Molecular Compounds)\\nJudiciary\\n70710101- Chemical technology of inorganic substances\\n70710101- Technology of silicate and hardly soluble nonmetallic materials;\\n70710101- Technology of mineral fertilizers\\n70710103 \\u2013 \\\"Chemical technology of high molecular weight compounds (technology of polymer production)\\n70710101 - Chemical technology (production of organic compounds)\\nPhD\\n02.00.11-\\\"Chemistry of colloids and membranes\\\"\\n02.00.13-\\\"Technology of inorganic substances and materials based on them\\\"\\n02.00.14-\\\"Technology of organic substances and materials based on them\\\"\\n02.00.16 \\u2013 Chemical technology, processes and devices of food industry\\n02.00.17 \\u2013 Technologies and biotechnologies for processing, storage and processing of agricultural and food products\"]},{\"key\":\"subjects\",\"title\":\"O\\u2018qitiladigan fanlar\",\"items\":[\"Bachelor\'s Degree:\\n1. Fundamentals of Construction of Manufacturing Enterprises\\n2. Bonded nitrogen production technology\\n3. Ammonium nitrate production technology\\n4. Modern methods of physicochemical analysis\\n5. Chemical technology of inorganic substances\\n6. Enterprise equipment\\n7. Thermal Processes and Devices in the Production of Silicate Materials\\n8. Fast Click Methods Technology\\n9. General Technology of Silicates\\n10. Prepress Technologies and Equipment\\n11. Pulp and papermaking technology\\n12. Technology of printing materials\\n13. Packaging Process Technologies and Equipment\\n14. Technology of silicate materials\\n15. Fundamentals of organic synthesis\\n16. Material hunos candy\\n17. Synthesis of organic matter\\n18. Organic Synthesis Equipment\\n19. Waste-free technologies in organic synthesis\\n20. Chemistry and technology of organic substances\\n21. Basics of Financing Organic Synthesis Enterprises\\n22. Synthetic Detergent Production Technology\\n23. Equipment for the production of synthetic detergents\\n24. Methods for the synthesis of monomers\\n25. Chemistry and Physics of High Molecular Compounds\\n26.Technology of coating-forming polymers\\n27.Classification of polymer materials and their fields of application\\n28.Technology of production of high molecular weight compounds\\n29.Chemistry\\n30.Chemistry (general and inorganic chemistry, analytical chemistry, physical-colloid chemistry)\\n31.Analytical and physical-colloid chemistry\\n32.Organic cumin\\n33.Construction chemistry\\n34.Organic and physical chemistry in construction\\n35Physico-colloid chemistry\\n36.Physical chemistry\\nJudiciary\\n1. Technological processes in the production of silicate materials\\n2. Theory and technological calculations of the production of mineral fertilizers\\n3. Theory and Technological Accounts of the Production of Inorganic Substances\\n4. Theory and technological calculations of the production of synthesized gases\\n5. Theory and technological calculations of bonded nitrogen production\\n6. Chemical technology of mineral fertilizers\\/ Chemical technology of potash salts\\n7. Chemistry and Technology of Element Organic Compounds\\n8. Adjustment of structure and properties in the manufacturing process of high-molecular compounds\\n9. Theoretical foundations of chemistry of high molecular weight compounds\\n10. Chemistry and technology of methane-based syntheses\\n11. Chemical theoretical foundations of coating-forming polymers\\n12. Technology of organic substances and materials based on them\\n13. Catalytic processes in the technology of obtaining organic products\\n14. Fundamentals of Physics and Mechanics of High Molecular Compounds\",\"Textbooks\\nTEXTBOOKS AND MANUALS\\n1. V.N.Akhmedov, Z.Kh.Rayimov, G.A.Gafurova.\\\" Terephthalic acid derivatives\\\". Monograph, Eastern-Bukhara Publishing House, Bukhara-2022.\\n2. Nurilloyev Zafar Ismatilloyevich, Asrayev Zafar Rizakulovich, Khojiyev Azizjon Kholmurodovich. \\\"Problems of general and inorganic chemistry and methods of their solution\\\" electronic textbook. DGU No. 40483.\\n3. Makhmudov Rafiq Amonovich, Shukrullaev Javohir Aibek ugli. \\\"Modern methods of physical and chemical analysis\\\". DGU No. 23886.\\n4. R.A.MAkhmudov, Ch.K.Khayrullayev, S.A.Niyozov, M.F.Haydarova, Z.M. Kamolova. \\\"Theory and Technological Accounts of Bonded Nitrogen Production.\\\" Textbook, ISBN 978-9943-9338-9-7. HOPE Publishing, 2023.\\n5. R.A.MAkhmudov, Z.M. Kamolova, S.A.Niyozov.\\\" Technology of Bonded Nitrogen and Nitrogen Fertilizers\\\". Monograph, UDK.667.664.3. 2024 6\\n. Niyozova N.R., Khuzhakulov K.R. \\\"Modification and application of synthetic oils in leather industry\\\". Monograph. ISBN 978-9943-8785-1-8. HOPE Publishing, 2023 7\\n. Sadirova S.N., Temirova M.I. Monograph, \\\"Effective technological approach in processing Karakul skins\\\". HOPE Publishing 2023.\\n8. Khaidarov A.A.\\\" \