ISSN: 2660-5643. Website: scholarzest.com. Spain-2024. Vol.5. P. 13-14.\\n7. Khamidov M.K., Balla D., Hamidov A.M., collector-drainage water in saline and arid irrigation areas for adaptation to climate change. 2020. IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science 422(1),012121\\n8. Khamidov, M., Juraev, A., Atamuradov, B., Rustamova, K., Najmiddinov, A., & Nurbekov, A. (2022, July). Effects of deep softener and chemical compounds on mechanical compositions in heavy, difficult-to-ameliorate soils. In IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science (Vol. 1068, No. 1, p. 012017). IOP Publishing.\\n9. Khamidov M. K. et al. Efficiency of drip irrigation technology of cotton in the saline soils of Bukhara oasis \\/\\/BIO Web of Conferences. \\u2013 EDP Sciences, 2024. \\u2013 \\u0422. 103. \\u2013 \\u0421. 00019.\\n10. Kh Khamidov, M., Buriev, X. B., Juraev, A. K., Sharifov, F. K., & Isabaev, K. T. (2023, February). Efficiency of drip irrigation technology of cotton in saline soils of Bukhara oasis. In IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science (Vol. 1138, No. 1, p. 012007).\\n11. \\u0425\\u0430\\u043c\\u0438\\u0434\\u043e\\u0432 \\u041c.\\u0425.Influence of phytoremediation plants on soil salts \\/\\/ Innovative technologies in water management complex. \\u2013 Ukraine, Rovno, 2012. \\u2013 \\u0421. 32\\u201334.\\n12.Juraev A. K. et al. Effectiveness of cost-effective irrigation technologies in cultivation of winter wheat in saline soils \\/\\/AIP Conference Proceedings. \\u2013 AIP Publishing LLC, 2025. \\u2013 \\u0422. 3256. \\u2013 \\u2116. 1. \\u2013 \\u0421. 050039.\\n13. Juraev, A. Q., Juraev, U. A., Murodov, O. U., Atamuradov, B. N., Najmiddinov, M. M., & Ruziyeva, M. A. (2024). Investigating irrigation system by using drainage water in the cultivation of repeated millet crop. In BIO Web of Conferences (Vol. 103, p. 00014). EDP Sciences.\\n14. Juraev, A. K., Khamidov, M. K., Atamuradov, B. N., Murodov, O. U., Rustamova, K. B., & Najmiddinov, M. M. (2023, February). Effect of deep softeners on irrigation, salt washing and cotton yield on soils whose mechanical composition is heavy and meliorative status is difficult. In IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science (Vol. 1138, No. 1, p. 012006). IOP Publishing.\"]},{\"key\":\"cooperation\",\"title\":\"\\u0627\\u0644\\u062a\\u0639\\u0627\\u0648\\u0646\",\"items\":[\"International cooperation relations\\nIn order to fulfill the tasks set by the State Program for the implementation of the Action Strategy for five priority areas of development of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2017-2021 in the \\\"Year of Development of Science, Education and Digital Economy\\\", approved by the Decree of the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan dated March 2, 2020 No. UP-5953 Professor Khamidov Ahmad Mukhamadkhanovich was attracted to the department, where he teaches students and masters. And also the doctoral student of the Department of Irrigation and Melioration Ulugov Maruf Rustamovich came to an internship at the UNIVERSITY OF ORESOV RECTORATE INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS OFFICE in the Republic of Slovakia within the framework of the ERASMUS + STUDENT SHORT-TERM MOBILITY FOR TRAINEESHIP project.\\nThe Department of Irrigation and Melioration in the 2025-2026 academic year will train 4 professors and teachers at Istanbul Technical University in Turkey, a memorandum of cooperation in order to digitalize the process of higher education, to ensure the transfer of knowledge based on the widespread introduction of digital educational technologies, to form knowledge, competence, skills and qualifications, taking into account the individual characteristics of each student signing.\"]}]', 'قسم الري واستصلاح الأراضي', 'In connection with the change in the internal structure of the institute in 2024, the department \"Water resources management and melioration\" Department \"Irrigation and melioration \" was organized. According to the order of the rector of the Bukhara', '2026-07-26 00:16:43', '2026-07-27 06:31:48'),
